From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: drain a boot packet after opening the data path

The P4 in-band interrupt input is edge sensitive.  The C6 can queue its
BOOTUP packet before the host's interrupt path observes an edge, leaving a
non-zero RX position but no work scheduled.  Poll the receive queue once
after OPEN_DATA_PATH; normal traffic continues to use SDIO interrupts.

---
 sdio/esp_sdio.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdio/esp_sdio.c b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -8,2 +8,3 @@
 #include "utils.h"
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
@@ -800,5 +801,11 @@ static int esp_probe(struct sdio_func *func,
 	ret = generate_slave_intr(context, BIT(ESP_OPEN_DATA_PATH));
 	esp_info("OPEN_DATA_PATH write completed: ret=%d\n", ret);
+	if (!ret) {
+		/* The first C6 BOOTUP frame predates the initial producer snapshot. */
+		context->rx_byte_count = 0;
+		msleep(100);
+		esp_process_new_packet_intr(context->adapter);
+	}
 
 
 	esp_info("ESP SDIO probe completed\n");
